<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    conn.tower - test tools for the booster catch tower (Terminal Guidance) - and conn.tower_site,
    the towers of a game seen from the Space Center (list, state, spawn, remove, fly to).

    A SEPARATE ASSEMBLY ON PURPOSE, and one with no reference to KRPC.Bridge.Core: it is a
    ground-test tool, deployed on its own next to whatever Core and plugins the install
    already runs, and it must not depend on their version. If it fails to load, KSP skips
    it and every other conn.* service is untouched.

    Hard reference to KRPC.SpaceCenter for the same reason as Ident: PlaceV1 takes a
    SpaceCenter.Vessel and a SpaceCenter.ReferenceFrame, which a signature cannot get by
    reflection. conn.tower's procedures only: conn.tower_site (TowerSiteService, TowerSite*.cs)
    names vessels by persistentId strings and uses no type of KRPC.SpaceCenter (kRPC's GPLv3
    assembly), so its code depends on kRPC.Core alone and could move to an assembly without this
    reference.

    Excluded from build/verify (stub build): it only makes sense against the real game. Its pure
    files (HingeRestWatch, TowerLayoutDeclaration, TowerSiteGeometry, TowerSiteFormat, TowerPackage) are
    compiled and tested by build/tests/tower.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <AssemblyName>KRPC.Bridge.Tower</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>KRPC.Bridge.Tower</RootNamespace>
    <OutputPath>$(DistRoot)Plugins\</OutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(BridgeUseStubs)'!='true'">
    <Reference Include="$(KRPCPath)\KRPC.SpaceCenter.dll">
      <Name>KRPC.SpaceCenter</Name>
      <Private>False</Private>
    </Reference>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
